From: Macron <macron@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: Run at the top of the application priority band on
 macOS.

Every wait a Windows thread wakes from, every event it sets and every
input message goes through the server's one thread. macOS runs it as an
ordinary timeshare thread (priority 31), so it queues behind the game's
own busy threads, and whatever it was about to wake waits with it,
whatever that thread's priority.

Measured on an M3 with every core busy (tools/perf/sndload.c in Macron's
repository): a set event took a median 0.4 ms to wake a time-critical
thread, 23 ms at the 95th percentile, 54 ms at the 99th and up to 192 ms;
a wake that does not come through the server (WakeByAddressSingle) took
0.03 ms at most. In Deadlock, 11 of the 15 longest gaps between refills
of the sound buffer in a minute were its time-critical sound thread
waiting to be woken.

The server's thread now gets what the server gives a time-critical
thread of a normal process: not timeshare, importance 32 (priority 63).
MACRON_WINESERVER_PRIORITY=normal leaves it as it was.
---
diff --git a/server/thread.c b/server/thread.c
index bb9728f..9763c7c 100644
--- a/server/thread.c
+++ b/server/thread.c
@@ -220,6 +220,38 @@ static void apply_thread_priority( struct thread *thread )
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
 static unsigned int mach_ticks_per_second;
 
+/* Macron: the server runs at the top of the application priority band, where
+ * it puts a time-critical thread of a normal process. Every wait a Windows
+ * thread wakes from, every event it sets and every input message goes through
+ * this one thread. As an ordinary timeshare thread it queued behind the game's
+ * own busy threads: on an M3 with every core busy a set event took a median
+ * 0.4 ms to wake a time-critical thread, but 23 ms at the 95th percentile and
+ * up to 192 ms, against 0.03 ms at most for a wake that does not come through
+ * here. MACRON_WINESERVER_PRIORITY=normal leaves the thread as it was. */
+static void raise_server_priority(void)
+{
+    struct thread_extended_policy extended_policy;
+    struct thread_precedence_policy precedence_policy;
+    int latency_qos = LATENCY_QOS_TIER_UNSPECIFIED, throughput_qos = THROUGHPUT_QOS_TIER_UNSPECIFIED;
+    const char *setting = getenv( "MACRON_WINESERVER_PRIORITY" );
+    mach_port_t self;
+
+    if (setting && !strcmp( setting, "normal" )) return;
+
+    self = mach_thread_self();
+    extended_policy.timeshare = 0;
+    precedence_policy.importance = 32;  /* priority 63 */
+    thread_policy_set( self, THREAD_LATENCY_QOS_POLICY, (thread_policy_t)&latency_qos,
+                       THREAD_LATENCY_QOS_POLICY_COUNT );
+    thread_policy_set( self, THREAD_THROUGHPUT_QOS_POLICY, (thread_policy_t)&throughput_qos,
+                       THREAD_THROUGHPUT_QOS_POLICY_COUNT );
+    thread_policy_set( self, THREAD_EXTENDED_POLICY, (thread_policy_t)&extended_policy,
+                       THREAD_EXTENDED_POLICY_COUNT );
+    thread_policy_set( self, THREAD_PRECEDENCE_POLICY, (thread_policy_t)&precedence_policy,
+                       THREAD_PRECEDENCE_POLICY_COUNT );
+    mach_port_deallocate( mach_task_self(), self );
+}
+
 void init_threading(void)
 {
     struct mach_timebase_info tb_info;
@@ -232,6 +264,7 @@ void init_threading(void)
         const unsigned int best_guess = 24000000U;
         mach_ticks_per_second = best_guess;
     }
+    raise_server_priority();
 }
 
 static int get_mach_importance( int effective_priority )
